On Fri, 28 Jul 2006, azgor wrote:
>
> [1]: If you apply a greased figurine or stone-to-flesh a greased
> statue, it should become a greased monster. This would make the monster
> slippery and fast! "Your greased mumak called Whiskers moves like
> greased lightning!" - azgor

   I really like the idea of StoFing a greased statue to get a greased
monster; however, all it should really do is resist owlbear hugs. (Does
wearing a greased cloak currently protect against hugs, sticky mimics,
and tentacles? I'm pretty sure it does, but if not, there's a YANI I'd
like to see.)
   There should definitely be a "greased lightning" YAFM involving
greased shocking spheres, but I can't think what.
   Anyway, this greased-monster thing is probably too complicated a YANI
to make it into a patch. IMHO, of course. /I/ wouldn't want to try adding
new monster properties.

> [2]: Any coaligned unattended altar should become sanctuary for a
> priest character upon entering the room. - jmr

   Interesting. Makes sense. Maybe too unbalancing, though.

> [3]: Either the HoOA should have no effect on neutrals other than
> welding to your head (strict interpretation of "opposite") or it should
> have a chance of making you neutral if you are Law or Cha (loose
> interpretation).

   Huh. What does it do now, then? Surely one of those is the Right Thing.

> [4]: Sitting on gold should be comfortable, and exercise charisma, when
> polymorphed into a dragon. - SpeedEvil

   I dunno about exercising charisma (although I disagree with whoever
said that might be unbalancing; haven't we already had a million threads
debating charisma's in-game (lack of) effect?) --- but I like the idea
that dragons find sitting on gold comfortable. I might add that to my
"sitting" patch, sometime.


> [9]: Giants should be able to eat items made of bone as per "I'll grind
> his bones to make my bread" from 'Jack and the Beanstalk' - azgor

   That's like saying humans should be able to eat items made of wheat.
(I, being a dumb suburbanite, assume that raw wheat is either bad-tasting
or painful to eat. Corrections welcome.)

> [10]: One mumak is to mumakil as a mimic should be to mimicid.  :)  And
> genociding mimics should further be known as mimicide. - Grunt

   Uh... right.

> [13]: You should be able to attach a bell to a pet kitten/cat. This
> would cause monsters to be aggravated by the cat and be less likely to
> attack you. -azgor

   This suffers from the "interface overload" problem; if (a)pplying a
bell takes a direction, how do you ring it?

> [14]: Multilevel stores. - moussambani

   To answer someone's question elsethread about exits: Each level could
have an exit guarded by a "floorwalker" (new type of @), who'd act just
like a shopkeeper, except that you'd have to go to the real shopkeeper's
level to pay.
   Most likely too much work, again, but still a YANI I'd like to see.

